{"timestamp": "2026-01-12T22:54:18.771773", "level": "INFO", "event": "heuristic_architect_completed", "data": {"problem_analysis": "The problem involves jointly optimizing INA placement and worker-to-aggregator assignment to minimize iteration makespan under strict physical and topological constraints. Key challenges include respecting the INA switch budget, switch processing throughput limits, and link bandwidth capacities while ensuring valid routing assignments. The solution must balance load distribution across switches and links, avoiding bottlenecks at PS nodes and overloaded switches, leveraging precomputed shortest paths and network topology data.", "strategy_overview": "The solution is structured as a deterministic, constructive pipeline: first, prioritize and rank candidate switches for INA deployment based on topological centrality and job demand; second, assign workers to aggregation points using a greedy, constraint-aware routing strategy; finally, assemble the final solution using the computed placement and assignment mappings.", "function_count": 3, "functions": ["_determine_ina_placement_candidates", "_assign_workers_to_aggregation_points", "solve_with_heuristic"]}}
